    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000124407,
      "SummaryText": "This facility processes natural gas and natural gas liquids (NGLs) The facility's capacity is 140 MMSCFD. Feed to the plant is noted to be low in H2S, consistently less than 4 parts per million (ppm) by volume.\nField compressors stations feed the facility through gas gathering pipelines that operate at 900 psi. A single residue gas line exports the natural gas at 1,100 psi to the residue gas sales pipeline. NGLs are sent out of the facility via pipeline to NGL sales pipeline. Three 60,000-gallon NGL bullet tanks are in place but are only used when the sales line is out of service for temporary storage and will be empty in normal operations. NGL transfer rate capacity is approximately  11,000 barrels per day. Condensate is moved from the site via tank truck from one loading spot near the two 1,000-barrel tanks present on site."
    }
